{
  "conversation_lines": [
    {
      "turn_number": 1,
      "time": "2144-06-16 10:45:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Hi, I'm Dr. Lee. I understand you had a fall recently and your blood tests showed a very high muscle enzyme level?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 2,
      "time": "2144-06-16 10:46:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Yes, I fell about a week ago. I didn’t think it was serious, but I’ve been feeling weak in my arms and legs since then."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 3,
      "time": "2144-06-16 10:47:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "That makes sense. We call that rhabdomyolysis — when muscle breaks down and releases proteins into the blood. It can affect your kidneys."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 4,
      "time": "2144-06-16 10:48:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Oh no, my kidneys? I’ve been urinating less and my legs are swollen."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 5,
      "time": "2144-06-16 10:49:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, that’s concerning. Your kidney function tests are abnormal. We’ll give you IV fluids to help flush out the muscle proteins and protect your kidneys."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 6,
      "time": "2144-06-16 10:50:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Okay, that sounds good. But why am I so weak? Is it just from the fall?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 7,
      "time": "2144-06-16 10:51:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We’re not sure yet. The fall may have triggered it, but with your history of obesity and multiple blood clots, we need to check for other causes like muscle disease or medication side effects."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 8,
      "time": "2144-06-16 10:52:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I’ve been on blood thinners for years because of my clots. Could that be part of it?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 9,
      "time": "2144-06-16 10:53:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "It’s possible, but we’re more concerned about your muscle enzymes being so high. We’ll monitor your strength and may need a muscle biopsy later."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 10,
      "time": "2144-06-16 10:54:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "A biopsy? That sounds scary."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 11,
      "time": "2144-06-16 10:55:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "It’s a small procedure. We take a tiny piece of muscle to check for damage. It helps us know if this is toxic myopathy — muscle injury from meds or other causes."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 12,
      "time": "2144-06-16 10:56:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Okay, if it helps figure out what’s wrong, I’ll do it."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 13,
      "time": "2144-06-16 11:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We also noticed you’re running a low-grade fever and your white blood cell count is high. Any burning when you pee?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 14,
      "time": "2144-06-16 11:01:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Now that you mention it, yes, a little. And I’ve been going more often."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 15,
      "time": "2144-06-16 11:02:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "That suggests a urinary tract infection. We’ll start antibiotics once we confirm with a urine test."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 16,
      "time": "2144-06-16 11:03:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I’ve had UTIs before. They usually clear up with meds."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 17,
      "time": "2144-06-16 11:04:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, but we have to be careful with your kidneys already under stress. We’ll pick a safe antibiotic."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 18,
      "time": "2144-06-16 11:10:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Your chest X-ray shows some lung collapse at the base, and you’re on oxygen. Have you been coughing or short of breath?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 19,
      "time": "2144-06-16 11:11:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Yes, I’ve had a cough for a few weeks. Thought it was from my last pneumonia."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 20,
      "time": "2144-06-16 11:12:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "It might be lingering pneumonia. We’ll keep treating it and monitor your oxygen levels."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 21,
      "time": "2144-06-16 11:13:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I’ve been so tired. And my joints hurt, especially my knees."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 22,
      "time": "2144-06-16 11:14:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Your knee X-rays show arthritis, which is common with your weight. But we’ll make sure it’s not something else."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 23,
      "time": "2144-06-16 11:15:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I know I’m heavy, but I can’t exercise because of the pain."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 24,
      "time": "2144-06-16 11:16:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We’ll work with physical therapy when you’re stronger. Right now, we need to stabilize your kidneys and muscles."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 25,
      "time": "2144-06-17 09:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Good morning. Your urine test confirmed a UTI. We’re starting ceftriaxone to treat it."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 26,
      "time": "2144-06-17 09:01:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Is that safe for my kidneys?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 27,
      "time": "2144-06-17 09:02:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, we’ve adjusted the dose. Your kidney function is starting to improve with the IV fluids."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 28,
      "time": "2144-06-17 09:03:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "That’s a relief. I’ve been feeling a little less swollen today."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 29,
      "time": "2144-06-17 09:04:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Good. We also checked your sodium — it’s low. That can make you feel weak and confused. We’ll adjust your IV fluids to correct it slowly."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 30,
      "time": "2144-06-17 09:05:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I have been feeling a bit foggy. Is that from the low sodium?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 31,
      "time": "2144-06-17 09:06:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Possibly. We’ll monitor it closely. Rapid correction can be dangerous, so we’re going slow."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 32,
      "time": "2144-06-18 10:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We did a CT scan of your chest because you’re still hypoxic. It shows a small blood clot in your right lung — a pulmonary embolism."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 33,
      "time": "2144-06-18 10:01:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Another clot? But I’m on blood thinners!"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 34,
      "time": "2144-06-18 10:02:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Sometimes clots happen even on treatment, especially with your history. We’ll continue your anticoagulant and monitor closely."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 35,
      "time": "2144-06-18 10:03:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Will this affect my recovery?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 36,
      "time": "2144-06-18 10:04:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "It adds risk, but we’re managing it. Your oxygen levels are improving, so that’s a good sign."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 37,
      "time": "2144-06-19 09:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Your leg ultrasound showed no new clots, which is great. The fluid behind your knee is a Baker’s cyst, not dangerous."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 38,
      "time": "2144-06-19 09:01:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "That’s good. I was worried it was another clot."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 39,
      "time": "2144-06-19 09:02:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We’re also treating your pneumonia with antibiotics. Your cough should improve soon."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 40,
      "time": "2144-06-20 09:30:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Your blood cultures came back clean — no bacteria. That’s good news. The yeast from your swab is likely a vaginal infection, not systemic."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 41,
      "time": "2144-06-20 09:31:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "So the fever isn’t from a blood infection?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 42,
      "time": "2144-06-20 09:32:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "No, it’s likely from the UTI and pneumonia. Both are responding to treatment."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 43,
      "time": "2144-06-21 10:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We ruled out syphilis and Legionella — both tests were negative. Your pneumonia is likely the same one from before."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 44,
      "time": "2144-06-21 10:01:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "So nothing new?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 45,
      "time": "2144-06-21 10:02:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "No, just lingering effects. Your oxygen levels are better, so we’re weaning your supplemental oxygen."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 46,
      "time": "2144-06-25 09:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Your muscle strength is still low. We’re scheduling a muscle biopsy on day 15 to check for toxic myopathy."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 47,
      "time": "2144-06-25 09:01:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Is that still necessary if I’m improving?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 48,
      "time": "2144-06-25 09:02:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, because we need to know if your medications are harming your muscles. That way, we can prevent future episodes."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 49,
      "time": "2144-07-01 12:15:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We just did the muscle biopsy. It went well. You might have some soreness, but it should heal quickly."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 50,
      "time": "2144-07-01 12:16:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I’m glad that’s over. Do you think it will show something?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 51,
      "time": "2144-07-01 12:17:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We suspect toxic myopathy due to your meds and history. The results will confirm it and guide long-term treatment."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 52,
      "time": "2144-07-02 09:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Your kidney function has improved, and your muscle enzymes are coming down. That’s great progress."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 53,
      "time": "2144-07-02 09:01:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I feel stronger. Can I go home soon?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 54,
      "time": "2144-07-02 09:02:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We’re planning to discharge you tomorrow. You’ll need home oxygen for a few more days and follow-up with neurology and pulmonology."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 55,
      "time": "2144-07-02 09:03:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "And my UTI and pneumonia?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 56,
      "time": "2144-07-02 09:04:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Both are resolving. Finish the antibiotics at home. Watch for fever or worsening cough."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 57,
      "time": "2144-07-02 09:05:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "What about my joint pain and constipation?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 58,
      "time": "2144-07-02 09:06:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We’ve started a stool softener for constipation. For joint pain, physical therapy can help once you’re stronger."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 59,
      "time": "2144-07-02 09:07:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "And the yeast infection?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 60,
      "time": "2144-07-02 09:08:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We’ll prescribe antifungal cream. It should clear up in a week."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 61,
      "time": "2144-07-02 09:09:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Thank you. I’m ready to go home."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 62,
      "time": "2144-07-03 10:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Good morning. Your labs are stable. We’re discharging you today."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 63,
      "time": "2144-07-03 10:01:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Finally! What do I need to do at home?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 64,
      "time": "2144-07-03 10:02:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Continue oxygen as needed, finish all antibiotics, and use the antifungal cream. Follow up with your doctors in a week."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 65,
      "time": "2144-07-03 10:03:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "And my muscle weakness?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 66,
      "time": "2144-07-03 10:04:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "The biopsy will help us understand it better. In the meantime, gentle movement as tolerated."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 67,
      "time": "2144-07-03 10:05:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I’ll take it slow. Thank you for everything."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 68,
      "time": "2144-07-03 10:06:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You’re welcome. Call us if you have trouble breathing, chest pain, or fever. Take care."
    }
  ],
  "summary": {
    "admission_start": "2144-06-16 10:44:00",
    "admission_end": "2144-07-03 16:31:00",
    "summary_paragraph": "A woman with a history of morbid obesity, multiple pulmonary emboli, and recent pneumonia was admitted after a fall with elevated creatine kinase, indicating rhabdomyolysis. She developed acute kidney injury, hyponatremia, and weakness. Workup revealed a new pulmonary embolism, urinary tract infection, and persistent pneumonia. She was treated with IV fluids, antibiotics, anticoagulation, and supportive care. A muscle biopsy was performed to evaluate for toxic myopathy. Her condition improved over 18 days, with resolution of infection, stabilization of kidney function, and gradual strength recovery. She was discharged home on supplemental oxygen with plans for follow-up and outpatient management of her muscle disorder.",
    "problems": [
      "Rhabdomyolysis",
      "Acute kidney failure, unspecified",
      "Other pulmonary embolism and infarction",
      "Urinary tract infection, site not specified",
      "Pneumonia, organism unspecified",
      "Toxic myopathy",
      "Hyposmolality and/or hyponatremia",
      "Myalgia and myositis, unspecified",
      "Morbid obesity",
      "Unspecified essential hypertension",
      "Hypoxemia",
      "Nonspecific low blood pressure reading",
      "Constipation, unspecified",
      "Anemia, unspecified",
      "Edema",
